  "summary": "Chapter 1 supplies the fiber maximum, its ramification-adjusted Lelong formula and the weighted pullback of finite measures. Chapter 16 applies these tools to ordinary and ideal envelopes below pulled-back obstacles, the degree-scaled polar model embedding and a mass-preserving 1-Lipschitz averaging retraction. It identifies the closed complete original-base subspace in every compact surjective curve map. The cubic analytic example shows that averaging need not be nearest. General P01/P17 and all 40 open assessment scopes remain open at their existing scopes.",
